<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
	Entitlements applied when the macOS bundle is code signed.

	Two entitlements are required, both not optional.

	automation.apple-events: the hardened runtime (which Tauri turns on as soon
	as a signing identity is configured) blocks sending Apple events to other
	applications unless this is declared. The Computer Use tool drives other
	apps through System Events, so without it a signed build would work
	unsigned and fail the moment it is signed.

	device.audio-input: the hardened runtime also blocks microphone access
	unless this is declared. Without it WebKit rejects getUserMedia outright
	with NotAllowedError, before the request ever reaches the TCC prompt — so
	the app never appears in Privacy & Security → Microphone and a manually
	granted permission cannot help. NSMicrophoneUsageDescription in Info.plist
	only supplies the prompt text; this entitlement is what allows the request.

	Screen Recording needs no entitlement — that is a pure TCC grant, requested
	at runtime with NSScreenCaptureUsageDescription (see Info.plist).
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.security.automation.apple-events</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
